---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import ContactEmail from "../../components/ContactEmail.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Corrections, removal & data rights — Open Editors Plus"
  path="corrections"
  description="Request correction or removal of your editorial-board record in Open Editors Plus, or report a data error. No reason required, no charge; acknowledged within 5 business days."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Corrections & data rights", url: "corrections" }]}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Corrections, removal &amp; data rights</h1>
    <p class="text-text-secondary text-lg mb-10">
      If you are listed in Open Editors Plus, you control whether and how your
      record appears. You can have it corrected, removed entirely, or object to
      it being processed — no reason required, and no charge.
    </p>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-8">
      <!-- How to request -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-6 mb-4">How to make a request</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Email the data-protection contact with your <strong>name</strong> as it
          appears in the data and the <strong>journal(s)</strong> you are (or were)
          listed for, and tell us what you would like done — correction, removal,
          or objection to processing:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-dim border border-border rounded-lg p-5 mb-4">
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Contact:</span>
            <ContactEmail subject="Open Editors Plus — correction / removal request" />
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-text-secondary space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li><strong>No reason required.</strong> You do not need to justify a removal or objection.</li>
          <li><strong>No charge.</strong> Requests are always free.</li>
          <li><strong>Removal is complete.</strong> If you ask for removal, your record is dropped in full — not merely hidden.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- What happens next -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">What happens next</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
          <div class="bg-white border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-800 mb-1">5 business days</div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">We acknowledge your request and confirm what we understood you to be asking.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-800 mb-1">30 days</div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">We action the correction or removal, and confirm back to you once it is done.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
          The change then propagates to the next versioned
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19590816" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zenodo</a>
          release and to the online <a href="/explore" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Explorer</a>,
          so the correction reaches everyone who uses the dataset going forward.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Report a data error -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Just want to report an error?</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If something about your record is simply <em>inaccurate</em> — a wrong
          affiliation, a misspelled name, a role that has changed — and you would
          like it fixed rather than removed, you can flag it the same way: email
          the data-protection contact
          (<ContactEmail subject="Open Editors Plus — data error report" />)
          with your name and the journal(s) concerned.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Honest limitation about CC0 copies -->
      <section>
        <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-amber-900 text-sm mb-1">One honest limitation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 leading-relaxed">
            Removing your record deletes it from the Open Editors Plus release, the
            Explorer, and all future versions we publish. Because earlier versions
            are distributed openly under CC0, we cannot recall copies that other
            people have already downloaded or redistributed elsewhere. We remove
            what is within our control and stop republishing your record; we cannot
            control independent third-party copies of prior releases.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Commitment / cross-link -->
      <section>
        <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-sm">
          The dataset is a permanent public deposit
          (<a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19590816" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19590816</a>),
          and we will keep a working contact address published for the life of that
          deposit so this route stays open. For what data the project holds, the
          named data controller, and the legal basis for processing, see the
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Privacy &amp; Data Protection</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
